 278:           # acceptance runs never touch it. So every Claude-territory item that builds dirties a
 279:           # Lovable-territory file it never wrote, and this guard fails a pull request for a change
 280:           # nobody made. The guard protects AUTHORED code; derived output has no author to protect,
 281:           # and the next build overwrites a hand edit anyway. One exemption here replaces a
